    <briefdescription>
<para>Registers a new restart field. <linebreak/>
Example usage: </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>call <ref refid="interfacefms2__io__mod_1_1register__restart__field" kindref="compound">register_restart_field</ref>(fileobj, &quot;temperature&quot;, data, (/&quot;lon&quot;, &quot;time&quot;/) )</para><para>Creates a restart variable and stores a pointer to the data.</para><para>This differs from the <ref refid="interfacefms2__io__mod_1_1register__field" kindref="compound">register_field</ref> interface in that registered restart fields are stored in the fileobj and can be easily read/written via a call to the read_restart/write_restart interfaces.</para><para><simplesect kind="note"><para>For individual documentation on the listed routines, please see the appropriate helper module. For netcdf files with a structured domain: <ref refid="group__fms__netcdf__domain__io__mod" kindref="compound">fms_netcdf_domain_io_mod</ref>. For netcdf files with an unstructured domain: <ref refid="group__fms__netcdf__unstructured__domain__io__mod" kindref="compound">fms_netcdf_unstructured_domain_io_mod</ref>. For generic netcdf: <ref refid="group__netcdf__io__mod" kindref="compound">netcdf_io_mod</ref>. </para></simplesect>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
